e here on e5 the knight  could recapture and then depending on  where black goes to sometimes we'll see  Knight to d7 trying to attack this  Knight but White has a  pretty interesting sacrifice here if  just Knight takes on f7 King takes and  then Queen up here to a tribe this is  check also for King attacking the knight  here on d5 so black would be forced  unless you want to go down a ton of  material to play King to e6 to hold on  to this material you can see although  black is up in material  he definitely has an exposed King and  White's gonna have a fun time choosing  this King around for the rest game  doesn't matter if it's Bishop to c4 just  pinning down the Knights whether it  wants to be just getting this dark  square Bishop involved castling on the  Queen side getting a rook here on e 1 to  start attacking there's not a lot of  great ways that black can continue and  still feel safe so in the game we see  Bob Fisher bring his Bishop down here to  g4 Bishop to e2 trying to stop some of  that pressure from the bishop pawn to e6  and then castle on the King side for  Spassky Fischer continues with Bishop to  e7 written to castle on the King side  pawn to h3 forcing the Bishop back here  pawn to c4 forcing the knight to come  back here to be six-night c3 symbol  development move castle on the King side  Bishop here to e3 pawn down to d5 upon  up here to c5 did have the option if he  wanted to exchange in the center bring  his rook over here to see one but  instead opted to try to just push in and  stop a lot of the squares that Bobby  Fischer could go to try to just choke  his opponent Bishop comes down here in  exchanges here on f3 a lot of times you  won't see a player exchange giving up  his Bishop for a Knights but recognizing  in this position specifically the  Knights just so strong controlling both  of the dark squares in the center of the  board so Bobby Fischer decides to go  ahead and exchange his knights for the  bishop also recognizing that this 